From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <noreply@xe.invalid>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 20:28:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/50] viz: VideoConferenceMatcher yields to other animating content

VideoConferenceMatcher (enabled for every desktop root compositor frame
sink, and on Android) lowered the display frame interval to the fastest
video's interval whenever two or more videos had updated recently, without
looking at anything else in the window: a page animating at 60 fps next to
two 30 fps videos (or an app drawing guests that play videos) dropped to
30 Hz.

FrameIntervalDecider now keeps a short history per drawn frame sink: whether
it submitted a new frame in each of the last 8 aggregations that drew it
(frame_time changed), and a smoothed interval between its new frames. For
sinks that are not video-only (video-only = has_only_content_frame_interval_
updates with only kVideo content intervals) it fills two new
FrameIntervalMatcher::Inputs fields:
- has_continuous_non_video_updates: a new frame in at least 7 of the last
  8 aggregations. This is relative to the display, because an animation
  that takes every frame follows a lowered display rate down (at 30 Hz a
  60 fps scene also updates at 30), so its absolute rate cannot be used.
- fastest_non_video_update_interval: the shortest smoothed interval of a
  sink that is still updating (its last frame no older than twice that
  interval, at least 3 intervals seen).
VideoConferenceMatcher returns no match if either says other content
updates on every display frame or faster than the videos. History entries
not drawn for 120 aggregations are dropped.

Behind kVideoConferenceMatcherYieldsToAnimation (enabled by default);

Tests: FrameIntervalMatchersTest.VideoConferenceYieldsToOtherContent,
FrameIntervalDeciderTest.VideoConferenceYieldsToAnimatingScene (two 30 fps
video sinks + a 60 fps scene keep the default rate; scene stops -> 30 Hz;
scene animates again -> default; only the videos -> 30 Hz). viz_unittests
*FrameInterval*, *SurfaceAggregator*, *Display* pass.

Measured (Release, Wayland): two <controlledframe> guests playing a 30 fps
video, embedder rAF: animating scene 58.0 (29.8 with the feature off), no
animation 31.1 (29.8 off); 16 / 32 real public pages without capture: scene
58 / 57 (29 before).
---
